Package: makimiru
Version: @VERSION@
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: gjs, libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libgtk-3-0t64, libgtksourceview-4-0, libevdocument3-4t64, libevview3-3t64, libgstreamer1.0-0, libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-0, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0, libharfbuzz0b, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, gir1.2-pango-1.0, gir1.2-webkit2-4.1, gir1.2-gtksource-4, gir1.2-evince-3.0, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gir1.2-gst-plugins-base-1.0, gir1.2-soup-3.0, gstreamer1.0-gtk3, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, default-dbus-session-bus | dbus-session-bus, shared-mime-info, systemd, xvfb, gir1.2-gnomedesktop-3.0
Recommends: nautilus, python3-nautilus
Suggests: gir1.2-lokdocview-0.1
Maintainer: Marty Fox <9006614+MartyFox@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/MartyFox/makimiru
Description: Interactive 3D model preview and thumbnails for GNOME
 MakiMiru adds spacebar Quick-Look-style preview and file-manager grid
 thumbnails for STL, 3MF, and OBJ 3D model files to GNOME Files
 (Nautilus). It is a fork of GNOME Sushi that adds one 3D viewer module
 plus a standalone thumbnailer, installed alongside the system Sushi
 package without modifying or replacing it.
 .
 The thumbnailer, its registration and a MIME type declaration for .obj
 files are installed system-wide and work immediately after install.
 The spacebar previewer needs one per-user D-Bus registration, which is
 written automatically and unprivileged the next time each user logs in
 to a graphical session (see /usr/libexec/makimiru-activate-user).
 Removing the package reverts it for every local user.
 .
 makimiru-pregen builds thumbnails for whole folders ahead of time, and
 with python3-nautilus installed, Files offers the same as "Generate 3D
 Thumbnails" in a folder's right-click menu.
